    "### 4.2b — MPNN1 & MPNN2 checkpointed eval (graph models)\n",
    "\n",
    "MPNN is a graph model, so it is *not* in `get_paper_models()` — it consumes SMILES (plus external features for MPNN2), not the precomputed fingerprint matrices. This cell runs the same checkpointed `model_validation` pipeline for the two graph models and appends their rows to the **same** `section4_*` checkpoint files, under featureset labels `graph` (MPNN1) and `graph_rdkit` (MPNN2), so Section 5 picks them up automatically.\n",
    "\n",
    "- **X-encoding** — SMILES are packed into `X` so `cross_val_score`'s row-splits keep SMILES (+features) aligned. MPNN1 `X=(n,1)`; MPNN2 `X=(n,1+316)` object array (col 0 = SMILES, cols 1: = the `'rdkit'` featureset's RobustScaler'd rmoldes matrix — reused, not re-featurized).\n",
    "- **SMILES/y identical across featuresets** for a given endpoint (the shuffle+split random_states depend only on `n`), so we read SMILES/y from the `fcfp4` split and the rmoldes features from the `rdkit` split — they stay row-aligned.\n",
    "- **Full vs Sample flag** — the paper did a single split / no CV. We deviate to get a boxplot distribution via `model_validation`. `MPNN_MODE='sample'` is a fast undertrained *preview* (2×1 folds, 20 epochs); `'full'` is the real 5×3 / 30-epoch run (~100 min). `n_jobs=1` always (chemprop parallelizes internally; macOS `spawn` breaks nested workers).\n",
    "- **Mode is recorded per row** (`mpnn_mode` column) and **`'full'` supersedes `'sample'`**: before running, any existing MPNN key whose stored mode is *weaker* than `MPNN_MODE` is invalidated so it recomputes; equal-or-stronger keys are skipped. So a cheap `'sample'` preview never blocks the real `'full'` run, and re-running `'sample'` never clobbers an existing `'full'` result."
   ]
  },
